.TH HWDP 1 "2026" "hwdp" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hwdp \- hardware display-profile detection, layout, and autoscale suite
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hwdp
recognises which monitors are present and lays out / autoscales the workspace
for them, keyed on the HARDWARE (an EDID-derived display-profile id), never on
a hostname. It is a suite of five tools installed on
.BR PATH ;
there is no eponymous
.B hwdp
command. It is environment-agnostic: it works under X11 or a wlroots compositor,
and hardcodes no downstream tool \(em everything session-specific is a HOOK or a
pluggable BACKEND an integrator fills.
.SH TOOLS
.TP
.B hwprofile
Detect hardware/substrate capabilities (a second Bluetooth adapter, an NVIDIA
GPU, the chassis, a btrfs root) into a sticky, fingerprinted profile so a
consumer gates on WHAT THE BOX HAS, not its hostname. A record is recomputed
only when its hardware fingerprint changes, so a hand edit survives. The profile
file path is the seam
.BR HWPROFILE ;
point it and the reader at one path.
.TP
.B kanshi-autoscale
Pick or synthesize the kanshi layout for the connected monitor set and fill each
output's scale from panel DPI. Subcommands:
.BR hwdp " (the display-profile id), " shape " (single/triple), " uiprofile
(per-display UI sizing lines a consumer sources),
.BR capture .
.TP
.B kanshi-mgr
Own kanshi's lifecycle in a session (supervise-or-nudge via
.BR flock ),
regenerate the config through
.BR kanshi-autoscale ,
and re-apply on compositor-config changes. It fires display-change HOOKS from
.IR <root>/<edge>.d/* " (edges: " pre ", " changed )
so an integrator wires reactions; it knows nothing of any specific compositor
tool. Hook roots:
.BR HWDP_HOOK_ROOT " (default ~/.config/hwdp/hooks), " HWDP_MACHINE_HOOKS
(default /etc/hwdp/hooks).
.TP
.B display-geometry
Print one line per enabled output \(em
.I NAME MODE_W MODE_H TRANSFORM SCALE POS_X POS_Y LOG_W LOG_H ORIENTATION
\(em from
.B wlr-randr
(wlroots),
.B xrandr
(X11), or a richer backend plugged in via
.BR HWDP_GEOM_BACKEND .
Settles by default (samples until the layout holds still);
.B \-\-now
prints one snapshot.
.TP
.B run-scaled
Magnify a single application via a nested
.B gamescope
window (renders at a size/scale and upscales), windowed or fullscreen.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/hwdp/hooks/<edge>.d/*
User display-change hooks run by kanshi-mgr.
.TP
.I ~/.config/kanshi/{profiles,auto-scale}
kanshi-autoscale's layout templates and sticky per-panel scale overrides.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HWPROFILE
Path to the capability profile file (writer + reader share it).
.TP
.B HWDP_HOOK_ROOT ", " HWDP_MACHINE_HOOKS
Roots for kanshi-mgr's display-change hooks.
.TP
.B HWDP_GEOM_BACKEND
An executable that replaces display-geometry's built-in backends wholesale.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kanshi (1),
.BR wlr-randr (1),
.BR gamescope (1)
